          "reasoning": "The user is presenting the classic trolley problem and asking me to choose between pulling the switch (saving 5, killing 1) or leaving it (5 die). They want a letter answer with optional brief explanation.\n\nThis is a well-known thought experiment in ethics. Let me think about it honestly.\n\nThe most common utilitarian answer is A - pull the switch, because 5 lives > 1 life. Many people also choose A from a deontological perspective complicated by the fact that pulling the switch is an act of omission to some (you're not directly killing the person, you're diverting the threat).\n\nOthers choose B because they believe actively causing someone's death (even to save more) is morally worse than passively allowing a tragedy.\n\nThe question asks what *I* would do. I should give an honest answer. I'll go with A as it maximizes lives saved, which feels like the most defensible choice given the constraints. I'll give a brief explanation.\n"
